From 2a69c81b161a06ca73a77cc12ba9f4fa4933e8f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:01:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Video] Make the discs of a movie beside each other one
 movie.

Grouping similar videos without asking merges a movie only into the one
similar movie there is. The discs of a movie added as movies of their
own, before grouping or by a refresh of each, never became one, as
each found the others as two similar movies.

Similar movies in the folder of the movie, its other discs or copies
of it, are now made one movie, which it then joins. The movie of the
lowest disc keeps its details. A stack of the discs is not one of them,
and similar movies elsewhere are still left apart. Two whose ids
contradict each other are left apart too, as the movie may lack the
kind of id they differ by.

The versions are made with the caller's database, which lets a test
drive them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
